#!/bin/sh
# armtix-screen on|off|toggle|status|apply [--save]
#   on / off / toggle  switch the phone screen now (--save: also make it the
#                      default at boot, in /etc/armtix/screen.conf)
#   apply              switch to what /etc/armtix/screen.conf says
#   status             print on/off
# Inside a sway session the output is powered off through sway (it keeps
# drawing nothing and comes back with `on`); without sway the framebuffer is
# blanked (display controller + panel powered down) and the backlight set to 0.
CONF=/etc/armtix/screen.conf
FB=/sys/class/graphics/fb0
BL=/sys/class/backlight/panel
SAVED_BL=/run/armtix-screen.brightness

usage() { echo "usage: armtix-screen on|off|toggle|status|apply [--save]" >&2; exit 1; }

conf_value() {
	v=$(sed -n 's/^[[:space:]]*SCREEN[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*"\{0,1\}\([a-zA-Z]*\).*/\1/p' "$CONF" 2>/dev/null | tail -1)
	case $v in off|OFF|0|no) echo off ;; *) echo on ;; esac
}

# A live sway IPC socket, if a sway session is running
sway_socket() {
	for s in /run/user/*/sway-ipc.*.sock; do
		[ -S "$s" ] || continue
		p=${s##*/sway-ipc.}	# <uid>.<pid>.sock
		p=${p#*.}
		p=${p%.sock}
		kill -0 "$p" 2>/dev/null && { echo "$s"; return 0; }
	done
	return 1
}

status() {
	if s=$(sway_socket); then
		SWAYSOCK=$s swaymsg -t get_outputs -r 2>/dev/null | grep -q '"power": true' && echo on || echo off
	elif [ "$(cat $FB/blank 2>/dev/null)" = 4 ] || [ "$(cat $BL/brightness 2>/dev/null)" = 0 ]; then
		echo off
	else
		echo on
	fi
}

need_root() {
	[ "$(id -u)" = 0 ] && return 0
	exec sudo -n "$0" "$@"
}

switch() {
	if s=$(sway_socket); then
		[ "$1" = on ] && pw=on || pw=off
		SWAYSOCK=$s swaymsg output '*' power $pw >/dev/null
		return
	fi
	need_root "$1"
	if [ "$1" = off ]; then
		b=$(cat $BL/brightness 2>/dev/null)
		[ -n "$b" ] && [ "$b" != 0 ] && echo "$b" > $SAVED_BL
		echo 0 > $BL/brightness 2>/dev/null
		echo 4 > $FB/blank     # FB_BLANK_POWERDOWN
	else
		echo 0 > $FB/blank     # FB_BLANK_UNBLANK
		b=$(cat $SAVED_BL 2>/dev/null)
		[ -n "$b" ] && [ "$b" != 0 ] || b=12800
		echo "$b" > $BL/brightness 2>/dev/null
	fi
}

save() {
	[ "$(id -u)" = 0 ] || exec sudo -n "$0" "$1" --save
	mkdir -p "${CONF%/*}"
	if grep -q '^[[:space:]]*SCREEN[[:space:]]*=' "$CONF" 2>/dev/null; then
		sed -i "s/^[[:space:]]*SCREEN[[:space:]]*=.*/SCREEN=$1/" "$CONF"
	else
		echo "SCREEN=$1" >> "$CONF"
	fi
}

cmd=$1; opt=$2
case $cmd in
	on|off) want=$cmd ;;
	toggle) [ "$(status)" = on ] && want=off || want=on ;;
	apply) want=$(conf_value) ;;
	status) status; exit 0 ;;
	*) usage ;;
esac
case $opt in
	--save) save "$want" ;;
	"") ;;
	*) usage ;;
esac
switch "$want"
